 function is sharp departure\nCan&#x27;t see buyers as fungible\n&amp; 2d Cir says must be rule\nmaking. But in dynamic field\nlike labor, change of mind may\nbe tolerated. Have some hesitancy\nabout affirming rule making\n\nDouglas, J. Came to think much\nof rule making at SEC\nbecause had settling effect\n&amp; got public participation\n\nStewart, J. Agree with NLRB – to extent\nwe dealt with rule making in\nWyman-Gordon we leaned [struck: to]\nagainst rule making. As to\nchange of mind, think Board\nhas authority under Act to\ndo so. Also agree on elimination\nof supervisors –\n\nOpen on whether\nBoard had enough of\nrecord to support finding\nof conflict here. WJB &amp; BRW\nagree – under Wyman-Gordon\nshouldn&#x27;t there be remand?\n\nWhite, J. Cong in 1947 did not purport to\nadopt all of NLRB &quot;managerial&quot;\nI disagree with 2d Cir that all\n&quot;managerial&quot; were excluded\nAlso disagree with</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term</p><h2>Teleprompter Corp. et al. v. Columbia Broadcasting System, Inc., et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/9540cf8d-76fa-4ab1-9703-8c9c984bd8cf.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term</p><h2>Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner &amp; Smith, Inc. v. Ware</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</butt