foreclosed, U [underlined: England].\n\nI wd go as far as S + W n\nfurther.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Harry A. Blackmun</p><h2>Speight, T/a Harem Book Store, et al. v. Slaton et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/ff93b176-2bc6-43e7-8db5-cad3a8a8a0f2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1417/1072\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Douglas, J. —\nWd n expand Y + H bey cts bare bones.\n≠ as Δ + civil field\nDuty . + fed cts + take\nStat is so gross\n\nDo n spin out a great\ndesign. This an outrageous case\nWrite narrowly.\nAm n in agmt wi + 5 H\n? discussion.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Harry A. Blackmun</p><h2>Speight, T/a Harem Book Store, et al. v. Slaton et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b1062165-4d74-4bc4-91a3-ab57213d7f1f.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1593/1437\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J.\nY stated fam prins 1) fed ct relu to\nenjoin St [underlined: crim] proc in its St, 2) comity\n3) potential for abrasive conflict. All old\nY applied\nHere civil proc in St is a party &amp; tries\nto term what St regards as crim activity\n#1 applies wi less force, poss. #2 ds.\n#3 too.\nWd n lump all civil cases tog.\n[struck: this on its face]\nNo poss of fed NC.\nIf this were a crim process, this\nwins &amp; [underlined: exceptions] to Y v H: harassment,\nirrep inj. Flagrant unconst on its face,\neven if [inserted: [underlined: n]] harassment.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Harry A. Blackmun</p><h2>O&#x27;Brien et al. v. Skinner, Sheriff, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/1733be1b-eca8-4ef5-afd1-8a4ef2f6ced8.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>11-9-73\n\nThe Chief Justice —\nMy choice here is unconstitutional\nbut is it irrational? That so, but\nMcDonald seems to OK.\nMcDon is n control, now\nSo —\n\nDouglas, J. —\nagree wi Burke\n\nBrennan, J. —\nMcDon tx mere regis voters\nGoosby also prob\nHere c/a says by probs tou for votg.\n\nStewart, J. — ? tentatv\nMcDon no control\nGoosby surf a subst fed?\nIse people n dif voters ie by law\nFold hd + ans\nRinaldi v Yeager</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Harry A. Blackmun</p><h2>Johnson, Administrator of Veterans&#x27; Affairs, et al. v. Robison</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</bu